abstract: >-
  Bash program, also an extension of the GitHub CLI, that pulls, commits, pushes, resets and clones
  every git repository under a folder, or those named from any folder, several at a time and several
  commands on one line, with one line of report for each repository that changed or needs attention.
  It never forces a push and never loses work: a conflict is undone
  at once, or settled with the version of the server first if asked, a file in the way of the server
  is moved aside and kept, nothing is committed unless asked for, a push waits for one confirmation,
  and a reset keeps the previous commit under a reference of its own.
